{
 "_comment": [
  "Hand-audited specification sufficiency labels, kept out of dataset.json.",
  "",
  "L1  the question and the relation signatures determine the target on their own.",
  "L2  they determine it for a reader who already knows a domain fact -- Maven's",
  "    three coordinates, the Atwater calorie factors, what context sensitivity",
  "    means in a points-to analysis. Fifteen of these carry that fact in the",
  "    dataset's `knowledge` field; the other ten expect the reader to have it.",
  "",
  "These labels are NOT part of a task. Nothing in the prompt shows them, and a",
  "solver is never told which tier a case is in. They live here rather than in",
  "dataset.json so that file holds only what a solver is given.",
  "",
  "Read them with care. The label is collinear with domain and with program",
  "complexity. evaluation/tier_report.py computes and prints the current counts",
  "instead of freezing them here, where they would go stale after relabelling.",
  "Slicing results on this label alone would mostly re-measure domain and",
  "complexity; report it controlled for both, or not at all.",
  "",
  "One person assigned every label."
 ],
